/-!
# Foundations: connected fibres, finite morphisms, regular local rings, canonical modules

This file collects eight foundational results used throughout the minimal model program.

* **Connected fibres.** A proper birational morphism `f : Y ⟶ Z` of varieties over a field `k`
  with `Z` normal has nonempty connected fibres; this is the topological half of Zariski's main
  theorem, `f_* 𝒪_Y = 𝒪_Z`.
* **Cohomology along a finite morphism.** For `f : Y ⟶ X` finite, `H^i(Y, 𝒢) ≅ H^i(X, f_* 𝒢)`
  naturally in the quasi-coherent `𝒪_Y`-module `𝒢`, a finite morphism being affine.
* **Regular local rings.** A regular local ring is a unique factorisation domain, its
  localizations are regular, and every Weil divisor on its spectrum is principal; conversely, if
  `x ∈ 𝔪` lies in no minimal prime and `A ⧸ (x)` is regular, then `A` is regular.
* **Finite over projective.** A separated scheme of finite type finite over a projective
  `k`-scheme is projective, and ample line bundles pull back to ample line bundles along finite
  morphisms.
* **Canonical modules under flat local extension.** For a flat local map `A → B` of Noetherian
  local rings with `𝔪_A B = 𝔪_B`, the derived base change of a normalized dualizing complex is
  normalized dualizing, `dim B = dim A`, and `ω_A ⊗_A B ≅ ω_B`. The comparison
  `H^n(K) ⊗_A B ⟶ H^n(K ⊗^L_A B)` is induced by flat tensor on complexes, is natural in the
  complexes and in coefficient rings, and computes the base change of Hom complexes out of
  finite free complexes.
* **Relative ample section algebras.** For `g : Z ⟶ Y` proper and `L` a `g`-ample invertible
  module, over each affine open `V ⊆ Y` the section ring of `L` on `g⁻¹(V)` is of finite type over
  `Γ(Y, V)` and `g⁻¹(V)` is its `Proj`, the canonical morphism sending the degree-zero fraction
  `b / s` to the ratio of sections `b / s`.
* **Relative semiample section algebras.** For `f : Y ⟶ S` projective over a locally Noetherian
  base and `L` an invertible module some positive power of which is generated by relative
  sections locally over `S`, the section algebra `⨁_{m ≥ 0} f_*(L^{⊗ m})` is locally of finite
  type: over each affine open `U ⊆ S`, `⨁_{m ≥ 0} Γ(f⁻¹(U), L^{⊗ m})` is a finitely generated
  `Γ(S, U)`-algebra.
* **Finite coefficient models.** Let `k₀` be a Noetherian ring and `K` a field which is a
  `k₀`-algebra. A finite diagram of `K`-schemes immersed into `ℙⁿ_K`, carrying a finite system of
  coherent modules and module maps along its arrows (indexed by a finite category `E` over the
  diagram's index category), descends to a finitely generated `k₀`-subalgebra `R ⊆ K`: there is a
  diagram of `R`-schemes immersed into `ℙⁿ_R` with a module system of the same shape whose base
  change along `Spec K ⟶ Spec R` recovers the given data. Open and closed immersions,
  isomorphisms, monomorphisms, epimorphisms, invertibility and triviality are retained. Effective
  Cartier divisors and rational sections on dense opens are instances of this data.

## Main definitions

* `MMP.flatDerivedExtensionScalarsIso`: along a flat ring map, derived extension of scalars of a
  complex is termwise extension of scalars.
* `MMP.flatHomologyTensorComparison`: the natural comparison `H^n(K) ⊗_A B ⟶ H^n(K ⊗^L_A B)`.
* `MMP.extendScalarsRestrictScalarsBaseChange`: the base change `B ⊗_A M' ⟶ B' ⊗_{A'} M'` of a
  commutative square of ring maps.
* `MMP.linearHomComplexBaseChange`: the base change `B ⊗_A Hom_A(F, N) ⟶ Hom_B(B ⊗_A F, B ⊗_A N)`
  of a Hom complex.

## Main results

* `MMP.Resolution.Bridges.isIso_app_and_isConnected_of_isBirationalMorphism` (second conjunct)
* `MMP.nonempty_cohomologyPushforwardIso_of_isFinite`
* `MMP.isRegularLocalRing_factorial_and_of_quotient_span_singleton`
* `MMP.Intersection.isProjectiveMorphism_and_isAmple_pullback_of_isFinite`
* `MMP.canonicalModule_derivedExtensionScalars_iso_of_flat`
* `MMP.isIso_projHomOfIsAmple_of_isProper`
* `MMP.exists_finset_closure_sectionRing_eq_top_of_isRelativelyAmple`
* `MMP.fg_sectionRing_restrict_of_isProjective`
* `MMP.exists_fg_subalgebra_model_of_finCategory`

## Implementation notes

* Connectedness of a fibre is `IsConnected (f ⁻¹' {z})` for the topological fibre; it is the
  second conjunct of `MMP.Resolution.Bridges.isIso_app_and_isConnected_of_isBirationalMorphism`.
* Cohomology is `Hfunctor`, the right derived functor of global sections; the comparison is
  `Stacks.AffineCohomologyResolution.cohomologyPushforwardIso`.
* Unique factorisation is stated as an `IsDomain` structure together with
  `UniqueFactorizationMonoid`. Principality of Weil divisors is proved one prime divisor at a
  time: every stalk of `Spec A` is regular, hence factorial, so the ideal sheaf of a prime
  divisor is an effective Cartier divisor, and its equation near the closed point is an equation
  on all of `Spec A`.
* Projectivity over `k` is `AlgebraicGeometry.IsProjectiveMorphism` of the structure morphism,
  and ampleness is `MMP.Intersection.IsAmple` (some positive power is very ample). The source
  works over `ℂ`; the base field here is arbitrary.
* Derived base change is `StacksDraft.PseudoCoherence.derivedExtensionScalars`. Along a flat map
  it is the degreewise extension of scalars, after lifting the module universe; the argument of
  [Stacks, Tag 0AWD] is run on that lift. The canonical module is the cohomology in degree `-d`,
  `d = dim A`, and it commutes with the exact functor `- ⊗_A B`. The comparison is the
  localization of the natural isomorphism `ShortComplex.mapHomologyIso` of cochain complexes,
  transported along the comparison of the total derived functor with termwise extension of
  scalars. Naturality in coefficient rings is stated for any commutative square of ring maps
  `τ ∘ f = f' ∘ σ` and a complex of `A'`-modules restricted to `A`; ring isomorphisms are the
  case of the source. The Hom complex of a chain complex `F` into `N` is
  `((linearYoneda A _).obj N).mapHomologicalComplex _` applied to `F.op`.
* The relative `Proj` of the section algebra is glued from the `Proj` of the section rings over
  the affine opens of `Y` (Stacks Tag 01NQ), so the relative statement is stated over each
  affine open, with the canonical morphism `Stacks.SectionRingProjMorphism.projHomOfIsAmple`.
* The semiample section algebra over an affine open `U` is the section ring
  `Stacks.GradedSections.sectionRing` of the restriction of `L` to `f⁻¹(U)`, with `Γ(S, U)`
  acting through `f^♯` into the degree-zero part (`Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.unitScalarEquiv`);
  finite generation is stated as a subring closure. Finitely many sections of one positive power
  `L^{⊗ D}` generate `L^{⊗ D}` on the quasi-compact `f⁻¹(U)`, so the high-degree pieces are
  generated by them in degree `D`, and every piece is finite over `Γ(S, U)` by coherence of
  proper direct images; `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProperAmpleCohomology.ringHomFiniteType_of_gen`
  turns these two facts into finite type.
* The finite diagram of the coefficient model is a functor `J ⥤ Over (Spec K)` from a finite
  category, and the module system is a lax system along `π : E ⥤ J`, unital and composable
  through `Scheme.Modules.pullbackId`, `pullbackComp` and `pullbackCongr`. The coefficient ring
  `k₀` is only required to be Noetherian, so that `R` is Noetherian and coherence makes sense on
  the model; the source takes `k₀` a field. The model is a stage of the limit `Spec K` of the
  spectra of finitely generated subalgebras (`MMP.CoefficientModels`).

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tags 0AY8, 089W, 00NU, 0AG0, 0AFS, 0AWD, 0AWE, 01PZ, 0B5T, 0EKI, 0C6J, 01CV]
* [J. Kollár, S. Mori, *Birational geometry of algebraic varieties*, §5]
* [R. Lazarsfeld, *Positivity in algebraic geometry I*, Corollary 1.2.28]
* [EGA IV₃, §8]
-/

universe u v w

